A crowd-pleasing party staple taken to the next level. Instead of cold deli meat slapped on rolls, these sliders feature slow-cooked caramelized onions, layers of shaved ham and Swiss cheese, tangy honey mustard, and a savory garlic-poppy seed butter glaze baked until golden, buttery, and molten.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a25658516/hawaiian-roll-slider-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

### Caramelized Onions
- 2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil
- 1 large sweet yellow onion, halved and thinly sliced
- Kosher salt, to taste

### Savory Poppy Seed Glaze
- 4 tablespoons (½ stick) unsalted butter, melted
- 1 tablespoon poppy seeds
- 2 cloves garlic, finely minced
- ½ teaspoon Worcestershire sauce

### Slider Assembly
- 24 sweet Hawaiian rolls (two 12-count packs, kept connected)
- ¼ cup mayonnaise
- ¼ cup honey mustard (or Dijon mustard)
- 2 lbs thinly sliced deli ham (honey-baked, smoked, or Black Forest)
- 1 lb sliced Swiss cheese (or Gruyère)

## Instructions

1. **Slowly Caramelize the Onions:** Heat olive oil in a wide skillet over medium heat. Add the sliced onions and a pinch of kosher salt. Reduce heat to medium-low. Cook slowly for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring every few minutes, until the onions soften, collapse, and turn sweet, jammy, and golden brown. Remove from heat and let cool for 5 minutes.
2. **Whisk the Glaze:** In a small bowl, whisk together the melted butter, poppy seeds, minced garlic, and Worcestershire sauce until well blended.
3. **Split and Prep the Rolls:** Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper. Without pulling individual rolls apart, use a long serrated bread knife to slice each 12-pack of Hawaiian rolls horizontally into top and bottom halves. Place the bottom halves side by side on the prepared baking sheet.
4. **Layer the Meats and Cheeses:** Spread the mayonnaise in an even layer across the cut bottom buns. Lay down half of the deli ham (1 lb), fold and ripple the Swiss cheese slices over the ham to cover completely, and top with the remaining ham (1 lb).
5. **Add Mustard and Onions:** Spread the honey mustard evenly over the top layer of ham. Scatter the warm caramelized onions across the mustard. Cap with the top roll sheets, pressing down lightly to settle the sandwiches.
6. **Butter Glaze:** Use a pastry brush to apply the garlic-poppy seed butter lavishly over the tops and sides of the buns, letting the savory butter seep into the crevices between rolls.
7. **Bake to Molten Perfection:** Slide into the oven and bake for 10 to 12 minutes. The sliders are ready when the Swiss cheese is completely melted and gooey and the roll tops are toasted, fragrant, and golden. (If the tops brown too quickly before the center cheese melts, tent loosely with a sheet of foil for the final few minutes).
8. **Slice and Serve:** Use a sharp knife or pizza wheel to cut along the seams into 24 individual sliders. Serve warm while the cheese pulls stretch.

## Notes

- **Make-Ahead Friendly:** Assemble the sliders completely up to 24 hours in advance (without brushing the butter glaze). Cover tightly with foil and refrigerate. When ready to bake, brush with the melted poppy seed butter and bake covered for 10 minutes, then uncover for 5 to 7 minutes until crisp.
- **Roast Turkey or Beef Variation:** Swap deli ham for smoked turkey breast or shaved roast beef with provolone cheese.
